ITEM B47 — Companion Node Audit & Top-Decile Relief Analysis
------------------------------------------------------------
1. Dual Criterion Audit across all 210 Populated Nodes:
   - Top-decile within-cell SRTM range cutoff (P90): 617.3 m.
   - Domain median offset: -2.85 m (range +-10m is [-12.85 m, +7.15 m]).
   - Nodes satisfying BOTH range >= 617.3 m AND offset in [-12.85, +7.15] m: EXACTLY 0 NODES.
2. Relaxation on the Record:
   - Extreme relief nodes along the Western Ghats escarpment naturally incur model smoothing offsets (|offset| >= 14 m).
   - Relaxing offset: The nearest top-decile relief node to the median is Node (15.00°N, 74.25°E) [i=10, j=3] (range = 652.2 m, offset = +14.00 m, 16.9 m from median, 32 villages, fully interior).
   - Relaxing relief: The highest-relief interior node strictly within +-10 m of median offset is Node (15.00°N, 74.50°E) [i=10, j=4] (range = 536.9 m, offset = -5.18 m, 2.3 m from median, 48 villages, fully interior).
3. Drop of Node (17.50, 74.00):
   - Node (17.50°N, 74.00°E) sits on row i = 0 and is bounded at 17.50°N by the domain mask, causing its areal mean to be evaluated over a truncated half-box. It is dropped. Interior node (15.00°N, 74.50°E) is retained.


